    <div class=3D"o-article__intro">
    <div class=3D"f-deck"><p>Jitish Kallat=E2=80=99s site-specific installa=
tion, <em>Public Notice 3</em>, returns to the Art Institute of Chicago=E2=
=80=99s Grand Staircase this fall after a 14-year hiatus. <br class=3D"soft=
break"></p></div>
  </div>
 =20
  <div class=3D"o-article__body o-blocks">
    <p>Initially unveiled on September 11, 2010, the work connects two sign=
ificant historical events separated by 108 years: the <a href=3D"https://ww=
w.artic.edu/articles/710/sisters-and-brothers-of-america-swami-vivekananda-=
in-chicago" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">First World=E2=80=99s Parliament of=
 Religions</a> which began on September 11, 1893, and the terrorist attacks=
 on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon on September 11, 2001. At the e=
arlier event, the World Parliament of Religions, held in an auditorium that=
 encompassed the area that today includes both the museum=E2=80=99s Fullert=
on Hall and Woman=E2=80=99s Board Grand Staircase, a young Hindu monk, Swam=
i Vivekananda electrified audiences with a <a href=3D"https://www.artic.edu=
/swami-vivekananda-and-his-1893-speech" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">powerfu=
l speech</a> calling for an end to religious fundamentalism, intolerance, a=
nd bigotry.&nbsp;<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>

<figure data-type=3D"image" data-title=3D"&lt;p&gt;Visitors experience &lt;=
em&gt;Public Notice 3&lt;/em&gt; in its inaugural installation on the Woman=
&amp;#8217;s Board Grand Staircase&lt;br class=3D&quot;softbreak&quot;&gt;&=
lt;/p&gt;" class=3D"m-media m-media--s o-blocks__block">
    <div class=3D"m-media__img" data-behavior=3D"fitText " data-platform=3D=
"">
                                                <img alt=3D"A photo of visi=
tors walking up the museum's Grand Staircase installed with Jitish Kallat's=
 Public Notice 3=E2=80=94neon text illuminates the staircase=E2=80=99s rise=
rs." class=3D"  " src=3D"https://artic-web.imgix.net/99f12203-3eb6-466a-b5f=
1-735ece49752c/D49151_062.jpg?rect=3D0%2C0%2C1024%2C695&amp;auto=3Dformat&a=
mp;q=3D1&amp;fit=3Dcrop&amp;crop=3Dfaces%2Ccenter&amp;w=3D750&amp;h=3D509&a=
mp;blur=3D1200&amp;sat=3D20" width=3D"1024" height=3D"695" data-pin-media=
=3D"https://artic-web.imgix.net/99f12203-3eb6-466a-b5f1-735ece49752c/D49151=
_062.jpg?rect=3D0%2C0%2C1024%2C695&amp;auto=3Dformat%2Ccompress&amp;q=3D80&=
amp;fit=3Dcrop&amp;crop=3Dfaces%2Ccenter&amp;w=3D600&amp;h=3D407">
                                                               =20
                                       =20
       =20
       =20
       =20
       =20
       =20
            </div>
            <figcaption>
                            <div class=3D"f-caption-title">
                    <div>
                                                    <p>Visitors experience =
<em>Public Notice 3</em> in its inaugural installation on the Woman=E2=80=
=99s Board Grand Staircase<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>
                                            </div>
                </div> <br>
                                            </figcaption>
    </figure>
<p>This very speech forms the basis of Kallat=E2=80=99s work, as the stairc=
ase risers are illuminated by Vivekananda=E2=80=99s words in five alternati=
ng colors=E2=80=94red, orange, yellow, blue, and green. These colors, borro=
wed from the decade-long advisory system of the US Department of Homeland S=
ecurity following the attacks of 9/11, formed a spectrum denoting terrorism=
 threat levels=E2=80=94from red for severe to green for low. Kallat transfo=
rms this motif of public vigilance into a radiant signal, reflecting Swami =
Vivekananda=E2=80=99s timeless and urgent plea for tolerance and universal =
acceptance.<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>

